## Output format
Produce a RevisionDelta with only new and modified elements. Do NOT restate the entire control structure.
The modified_responsibilities list must contain ONLY responsibilities you are CHANGING. The dismissed_gaps list should contain one-sentence justifications for any findings you chose not to address.

Return exactly one JSON object with this schema (all five top-level fields are
required; use an empty list when a field has no entries):

```json
{
  "new_responsibilities": [],
  "new_controlled_processes": [],
  "new_coordination_links": [],
  "modified_responsibilities": [],
  "dismissed_gaps": []
}
```

When adding a coordination link, return the complete nested link and mechanism
shape. This unrelated greenhouse example assumes `RESP-3` and `RESP-4` are
existing responsibilities and `PM-3-1` is the shared process-model part; the
IDs are references, not replacement prose:

```json
{
  "new_responsibilities": [],
  "new_controlled_processes": [],
  "new_coordination_links": [
    {
      "link_id": "CL-3",
      "source": "RESP-3",
      "target": "RESP-4",
      "shared_pm": "PM-3-1",
      "coordination_mechanism": {
        "cm_id": "CM-3",
        "description": "Share the current greenhouse temperature state",
